 - 2026-06-11: EIGHTH ARC-AGI-3 game first-solve via the PROVEN explore-first method (raises games-solved 7->8; monotonic +1 per the Incremental-Progress rule): exp4038 solved the 7th game (dc22-fdcac232). Apply the proven loop -- (1) active exploration OBSERVES transitions, (2) induce mechanic + goal predicate from OBSERVED transitions, (3) GAP-4 verifier validates the rule, (4) act -- to a NEW non-spatial-planning game from the win-condition survey not yet solved (AVOID vc33's spatial-planning trap -- that is exp4046's target). Honest no-solve is a COMPLETE verdict. Save the solve trace for exp4050 (ArcMemo v7 cross-game transfer). (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: eighth_game_solved_sb26-7fbdac44_at_action_9; results/experiment_4049_eighth_game_explore_first.json
 - 2026-06-11: ArcMemo v7: CROSS-GAME concept-library transfer (self-learning MANDATE; extends the exp4039 v6 within-game win): v6 compressed concepts into named abstractions and won WITHIN the milestone (59->18 actions). v7 tests the real self-learning claim -- does the library built from the 7 PRIOR solved games REDUCE the cost of solving a GENUINELY NEW 8th game (exp4049)? Seed exp4049's explore-first solver with the v6 library; measure action-count + induction-call reduction on the 8th game vs (a) a cold start and (b) v6's within-game-only memory. This is TRANSFER (across games), not replay (within one) -- the bar that distinguishes self-learning from caching. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: arcmemo_v7_no_cross_game_transfer_v7_not_cheaper_than_within_game_v6; results/experiment_4050_arcmemo_cross_game_transfer_v7.json
 - 2026-06-11: VERIFIER-REGISTRY + GAPS HYGIENE (infrastructure; reserved infra slot): bit-exact OFFLINE re-eval that reproduces the canonical GAP-4 ARC-1 (28/30) and ARC-2 numbers from cached candidates (zero codex, zero GGUF -- the regression guard); RECORD the .374 G1 off-ARC power outcome from exp4045 (update the GAP-CODE-EXEC-DEMOFIT ledger entry with the full-N CI -- did a stronger discriminator close it?); RECORD the G2 closed-loop outcome from exp4046 (did closed-loop grounding break the wall, or is there a sim2real ceiling gap to log?). Keeps ops/verifier_registry.yaml + ops/verifier_gaps.md the honest source of truth for what the verifier covers. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: gap4_reeval_bitexact_g1_g1_off_arc_power_pending_g2_g2_sim2real_ceiling_gap_logged_recorded; results/experiment_4051_verifier_registry_and_gaps_hygiene.json
+- 2026-06-11: Hardware continuity (consolidated; KV260 drive-toward-terminal per north-star §3): exp4040 loaded the carnot_ising overlay on KV260 but the board-latency-transcript step stayed BLOCKED -- this task drives that final terminal step (the overlay is now present; take the latency transcript over SSH). GateMate (openFPGALoader -c dirtyJtag --detect) + PolarFire (ssh polarfire) opportunistic. Per KV260 SSH-Not-SD-Card Discipline: SSH-reachability is the ONLY valid KV260 precondition. DISTINCT wall-clock timers per board (no shared-timestamp tautology). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: hardware_continuity_kv260_latency_transcript_landed_4052_gmreachable_detected_gatemate_idcode_pfreachable_ssh_continuity_recorded; results/experiment_4052_hardware_continuity.json
